cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "biofilm-processing: high-throughput biofilm phenotyping from brightfield timelapse microscopy"
abstract: >-
  A high-throughput pipeline for automated brightfield timelapse microscopy of
  96-well plates. Processes per-well TIFF stacks through registration,
  segmentation, colony tracking, and colony/whole-image feature extraction, with
  a PySide6 GUI and headless CLI tools.
type: software
version: 0.5.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/melsehna/biofilm-processing"
authors:
  - family-names: Mellick
    given-names: "Seh Na S."
    email: smellick@andrew.cmu.edu
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO: add ORCID
keywords:
  - biofilm
  - microscopy
  - image-analysis
  - phenotyping
  - colony-tracking
